## Deployment

{% if deploy_target == 'local' %}Local only for now (`docker compose up`). Cloud deploy flags coming next:
`--deploy=azure`, `--deploy=aws`, `--deploy=gcp-cloud-run`.{% elif deploy_target == 'azure' %}Azure App Service (Linux, container). Files in `infra/`:
- `infra/main.bicep` — ACR + App Service Plan + App Service + Postgres Flexible Server
- `infra/dev.bicepparam`, `infra/staging.bicepparam`, `infra/prod.bicepparam` — env-specific parameters

Deploy:
```bash
az login
az bicep build --file infra/main.bicep --outfile infra/main.json
az deployment group create --resource-group <rg> \
    --template-file infra/main.bicep \
    --parameters infra/dev.bicepparam
```

CD lives in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (push to `main` or manual dispatch).
Required secrets:
- `AZURE_TENANT_ID`, `AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` (OIDC federation)
- `AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP`{% elif deploy_target == 'azure-container-apps' %}Azure Container Apps. Deploy:
```bash
az login
az containerapp up --source . --resource-group <rg> --environment <env>
```{% endif %}

## Pre-commit hook

A `.githooks/pre-commit` script is bundled that runs the same smoke tests
CI does — locally, before each commit. To enable it once per checkout:

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
```

To bypass in an emergency (`--no-verify`).

## Secrets

Never commit secrets. `.env.example` shows the required variables. CI runs
[gitleaks](https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks) so accidental commits get
caught before they hit `main`.

